  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable tourism and bioculturality in UNESCO designated sites</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UNESCO Office in Mexico aims to recognize and promote cultural and natural heritage around UNESCO designated sites through sustainable tourism and sustainable use of natural resources. Specific plans will be developed in order to promote sustainable development through their alignment to Agenda 2030 and of the SDG&apos;s in order to foster tourism and the engagement of local communities in the conservation of natural and cultural resources. The links among stakeholders will be strengthened and their capacities improved. Science and local knowledge will be essential components of the projects.</narrative>
  </description>
